+\section*{1. The circuit exists before the switch}
+A light switch acts on an existing circuit. Its conductors, connections and load
+are already in place; operating the switch changes the conducting path.
+The computational principle is to prepare the connected structure before a
+request arrives, retain it, and let the request act through its gates.
+The response then pays for activation and propagation through that structure.
+
+A membrane holds operations, connections and reusable state behind an interface.
+Nesting places shared preparation around the operations that consume it.
+Levels can exchange signals through forward, bypass and return connections.
+Their number follows the object being realized. Depth is a construction
+parameter; an illustrative number of boxes carries no special significance.
+
