+The engineering meaning of immediate response is that construction has already
+been paid for when the gate changes. Propagation still has a duration.
+Hardware follows physical paths and switching dynamics. The current Vox
+realization follows interpreted instructions and memory accesses.
+Both descriptions separate preparation from activation.
+
+\section*{2. A persistent transformation}
+Write the membrane as a directed graph $G$, with parameters $p$, state $s$,
+gates $g$ and input $x$. Its contracts are
+\[
+ C=\operatorname{prepare}(G,p),\qquad
+ (s_{t+1},y_t)=\operatorname{activate}(C,s_t,g_t,x_t).
+\]
+The circuit $C$ survives the call. Its topology, operators, coefficients and
+storage remain available while the gates and signals change.
+The current payload is transformed through the prepared structure.
+Feedback requires a defined delay, scheduling rule or settling rule.
+
+\newpage
+\section*{3. Nesting moves work to its enclosing lifetime}
+Let $L$ denote loading, $P$ preparation, $A_t$ activation and $R_t$ output
+extraction. For $K$ requests sharing topology and parameters,
+\[
+ T_{\rm resident}=L+P+\sum_{t=1}^{K}(A_t+R_t),\qquad
+ T_{\rm cold}=\sum_{t=1}^{K}(L+P+A_t+R_t).
+\]
+Under these assumptions, retaining the circuit removes $(K-1)(L+P)$ from the
+repeated work. Residency exchanges retained storage for avoided reconstruction.
+
+Nesting also changes work inside an algorithm. An enclosing region prepares a
+factorization, table, graph or phase schedule once. Inner operations consume it.
+A search can preserve its enclosing state and roll back only a child's additions.
+These transformations can change the amount of work as well as its location.
+
+For alternative arms tried in order, the cost through the first decisive arm $j$
+is
+\[
+ T_j=\sum_{i<j}T_{{\rm reject},i}+T_{{\rm decide},j}.
+\]
+Cheap shape tests and fast rejection keep the preceding sum small. The practical
+ordering test measures each affected input family against its control.
+
