+\section*{5. A circuit retained across requests}
+The resident interface keeps the same IMASM machine alive. It invokes the
+module's preparation function once, then repeatedly invokes its activation
+function. Metadata supplies the port count, output address and counters.
+
+\begin{center}
+\begin{tikzpicture}[node distance=6mm]
+\node[box,text width=2.45cm] (load) {Load module\\resolve entry points};
+\node[box,text width=2.45cm,right=of load] (prep) {Prepare\\phases + signals};
+\node[box,text width=2.45cm,right=of prep] (wait) {Resident circuit\\await gate input};
+\node[box,text width=2.45cm,right=of wait] (act) {Activate\\propagate signals};
+\draw[active] (load)--(prep);
+\draw[active] (prep)--(wait);
+\draw[active] (wait)--(act);
+\draw[active] (act.south)--++(0,-.8)-|node[pos=.25,below,font=\small]{retain state; accept the next gates}(wait.south);
+\end{tikzpicture}
+\end{center}
+With standard-input streaming, preparation finishes before gate changes are
+read. The interactive record has one preparation followed by five activations:
+fresh input, a changed mask, feedback, clearing, and reactivation.
