+\section*{6. The depth-selected QFT circuit}
+The circuit has $N=2^d$ ports and $d$ transform levels. Depth is selected at
+module build time; the construction has run in Vox at $d=3,6,8$.
+The direct-transform checking runner accepts up to 4,096 ports.
+
+Input permutation and butterfly connections are compile-time data.
+Preparation supplies the phase table, normalization and cleared signal storage.
+Each connection records two source positions, sum and difference destinations,
+and a phase index. At stage width $w$, a butterfly computes
+\[
+ z=e^{2\pi i j/w}b,\qquad u=a+z,\qquad v=a-z.
+\]
+Readout applies $N^{-1/2}$. Storage contains $Nd/2$ butterfly records,
+$N/2$ phases, $N$ permutation entries and $N(d+1)$ complex signal slots.
+
