+
+Let $D(g_t)$ be the diagonal gate mask and $F_N$ the normalized positive-sign
+Fourier transform. The implemented source and readout are
+\[
+ x_t=\begin{cases}
+ D(g_t)\mathbf 1,&\text{fresh source},\\
+ D(g_t)y_{t-1},&\text{feedback source},
+ \end{cases}
+ \qquad y_t=F_Nx_t.
+\]
+The 64-bit gate mask repeats across ports when $N>64$.
+Feedback samples the preceding normalized output before the next sweep begins:
+the return path has one activation of delay.
+
+Every activation overwrites signal slots through a full butterfly sweep.
+Closing all input gates produces zero output, including after nonzero feedback.
+Guest activation uses fixed storage with no allocation or topology
+reconstruction. The host controller and Vox interpreter have their own
+allocation and execution costs.
+
+In ideal arithmetic, full-open feedback reapplies $F_N$:
+$F_N^2x[j]=x[-j\bmod N]$ and $F_N^4=I$, by summing Fourier phases over the
+intermediate index. Such feedback can cycle. The sampled return path gives
+this recurrent computation an explicit temporal meaning.
+
+\newpage
+\section*{7. Measurements and controls}
+Every output port is compared with a separately evaluated direct transform.
+For feedback, the reference propagates its own preceding expected output.
+Its componentwise absolute-error threshold is $10^{-10}$. The default cases
+exercise zero gates, changed masks, feedback, clearing and reactivation.
+Recorded maximum errors reach approximately $1.3\times10^{-15}$,
+$1.8\times10^{-14}$ and $1.3\times10^{-13}$ at 8, 64 and 256 ports.
+
+\small
+\begin{tabularx}{\linewidth}{@{}rrXXXX@{}}
+\toprule
+$d$&$N$&Preparation&Resident activation&Cold parse + prepare + activate&Cold / resident\\
+\midrule
+3&8&112.336 $\mu$s&545.599 $\mu$s&37.305347 ms&68.38$\times$\\
+6&64&755.225 $\mu$s&8.004777 ms&45.928677 ms&5.74$\times$\\
+8&256&23.401976 ms&39.995148 ms&103.725391 ms&2.59$\times$\\
+\bottomrule
+\end{tabularx}
+\normalsize
+Preparation is a single initial reading separate from loading. Activation and
+cold columns are medians of five executions with the same gate mask.
+Each cold execution starts with module text already in host memory, parses a
+new VM, prepares and activates. Each resident execution activates the existing
+prepared VM. Extraction, reference checking and printing follow the timer.
+
+These ratios measure avoided reconstruction for this path. The sequential
+propagation sweep still performs $O(N\log N)$ arithmetic. Increasing depth in
+this sweep also increases port count. A fixed-size topology experiment would
+isolate depth alone.
+
+\section*{8. Reproduction and connected extensions}
+From the Vox working directory:
+\begin{verbatim}
+./qft_circuit.sh 3
+./qft_circuit.sh 8
+./target/release/vox circuit \
+  membranes/qft_circuit/256/payload.elf.imasm --stdin
+\end{verbatim}
+Enter a hexadecimal mask per line, optionally followed by \code{:1} for feedback:
+\begin{verbatim}
+1
+0123456789abcdef
+ffffffffffffffff:1
+0
+\end{verbatim}
+End-of-file closes the controller. Complete-process examples use
+\code{./membrane_one.sh shor 2 21 12} or
+\code{./membrane_one.sh divisor 1125899906842624 360 97}.
+
+The general connected-membrane design admits prebound ports between multiple
+resident modules and gates spanning nonadjacent levels. Its QFT realization
+uses adjacent butterfly levels with a sampled output-to-input return path.
+Further routing realizations can retain the same contracts: explicit state
+ownership, defined feedback timing, and separate measurements of preparation,
+activation, propagation and extraction.
+
